- **Elements**: These are the building blocks of an HTML page. They include tags that define metadata, structure, and content of the page.
- **Attributes**: These provide additional information about HTML elements. For instance, an `a` element can have an `href` attribute, which specifies the URL to be linked.

Example of a basic HTML document:
```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>My Web Page</title>
</head>
<body>
    <h1>Welcome to My Web Page</h1>
    <p>This is a paragraph of text.</p>
    <a href="https://example.com">Link to Example</a>
</body>
</html>
```

2. **CSS (Cascading Style Sheets)**

CSS is used to style the layout and presentation of an HTML document. It controls the appearance and design of elements on a web page.

- **Properties**: These specify the look and formatting of HTML elements.
